olorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 601 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nRobinson Creek, Coal Creek, Wildhorse Creek, Willow Creek, West\nFork Willow Creek, Little Owl Creek and Owl Creek.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Northwestern Weld County.","ends":"2026-08-22T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9e428326a8704836f5ccedeb468ba10cbbe4822e.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9e428326a8704836f5ccedeb468ba10cbbe4822e.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 22 at 5:35PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 535 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from 5 miles northeast of Rockport to 7 miles\nnortheast of New Raymer, or extending from 33 miles northeast of Fort\nCollins to 30 miles west of Sterling, moving north at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nGrover, Pawnee Buttes, Hereford and Rockport.","ends":"2026-08-22T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Northeast Weld County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0077729709fb108d72cab7d0e970891c0910677a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0077729709fb108d72cab7d0e970891c0910677a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 22 at 5:12PM MDT until August 22 at 8:15PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 815 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 512 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area.\nBetween 0.5 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1.5 inches are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFort Lupton, Lochbuie and Wattenburg.","ends":"2026-08-22T20:15:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5b3a8c73dd9f8d2fed146c7cc5b4cd01b5968843.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5b3a8c73dd9f8d2fed146c7cc5b4cd01b5968843.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-22T23:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 222347 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 547 PM MDT Sat Aug 22 2026 FXUS65 KBOU 221850 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1250 PM MDT Sat Aug 22 2026 - Highest coverage of showers and storms expected today, along with a few severe storms and locally heavy rainfall this afternoon and evening. - Scattere","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-22T19:27:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Sunday... Scattered to numerous showers and storms, most with wetting rains, will push east from the mountains across the plains late this afternoon and evening. Humidity values will be moderate today, and then expect very good recovery tonight in all areas. Sunday w